  "sn35.124:1.2": "Ugga was the foremost in giving nice things (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/an1.253/en/sujato'>AN 1.253</a>), a quality exemplified at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.44/en/sujato'>AN 5.44</a>. This Ugga (“of Vesalī”) and the Uggata of the next discourse (“of Elephant Village” near Vesalī) are both said to have eight excellent qualities (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.21/en/sujato'>AN 8.21</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.22/en/sujato'>AN 8.22</a>). ",
